# sweep-identity.example -- owner identity for scripts/secret-sweep.sh
#
# The pre-push secret-sweep gate (scripts/secret-sweep.sh) needs the OWNER's
# real identity strings to detect owner PII (Telegram ID, emails, real name,
# machine home path) before anything reaches a public git history. Those strings
# are PII, so they are NOT embedded in the tracked script -- they live here, in
# an UNTRACKED machine-local file that the script sources at runtime.
#
# SETUP:
#   1. Copy this file to  ~/.dogany/sweep-identity
#        mkdir -p ~/.dogany
#        cp scripts/sweep-identity.example ~/.dogany/sweep-identity
#        chmod 600 ~/.dogany/sweep-identity
#   2. Replace every DUMMY value below with your real identity.
#   3. NEVER commit the filled-in file. It is machine-local only.
#      (The repo .gitignore also ignores a repo-relative ".sweep-identity"
#       override, but the canonical location is ~/.dogany/sweep-identity.)
#
# Each value is an ERE fragment passed to `grep -E`. Escape regex metacharacters
# as needed. All five vars are REQUIRED; if any is empty the owner-PII
# categories (cat2-5 and the owner-name part of cat9) are disabled with a loud
# warning and only the generic secret categories run.

# cat2 -- owner Telegram ID (numeric)
SWEEP_OWNER_TG_ID='1234567890'

# cat3 -- owner email(s). ERE alternation is fine, e.g. '(you|you.alt)@example'
SWEEP_OWNER_EMAIL_PAT='(you)@example'

# cat4 -- owner real name(s). Include native-script names, e.g. 'Your Name|이름'
SWEEP_OWNER_NAME_PAT='Your Name'

# cat5 -- owner machine home path prefix, e.g. '/Users/you' or '/home/you'
SWEEP_MACHINE_PATH='/Users/you'

# cat9 -- owner-name / login / hostname portion merged into the git-identity
# scan. ERE alternation of real name, login username, and machine hostname.
# The machine-local '@*.local' pattern is added by the script itself; do NOT
# repeat it here.
SWEEP_OWNER_IDENT_PAT='Your Name|you|your-host'
